I created `tests/repair.test.ts` covering `repairBuilding`'s three documented behaviors plus edge cases:

- Repairs an already-built building for half its original cost (hut: 10 → 5 wood deducted).
- Rounds up per resource for an odd cost (farm: 15 wood → 8, 5 stone → 3).
- Is a no-op when the settlement doesn't own that building (returns the same object, resources and buildings unchanged).
- Never takes a resource below 0 (3 wood with a 5 wood repair clamps to 0).
- Bonus: verifies the original settlement isn't mutated (the function returns a new object).

The first run surfaced a bug in my own test — I forgot to give the settlement a `hut` in the "short on resources" case, so the repair was correctly a no-op. Fixed by adding `buildings: ["hut"]`. `src/sim.ts` was left untouched.


